>> title: Pastry Cream
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: custard, vanilla, filling, stovetop, make-ahead
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: crème pâtissière, creme patissiere, custard filling, confectioner's custard
>> servings: 8
>> time: 2 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — two minutes at an actual boil or the starch never sets, and thirty seconds past that it catches and tastes scorched through

Heat @whole milk{2%cup}(480 mL), @vanilla bean{1%whole}(split, seeds scraped in) in a #saucepan{} until steaming.

Whisk @egg yolks{6%large}(110 g), @granulated sugar{2/3%cup}(135 g), @cornstarch{1/4%cup}(32 g), @table salt{1/4%tsp} until smooth.

Temper @&(~1)yolks{} with @&(~2)hot milk{}.

>> step: cook until it boils and thickens, 2 min
Cook @&(~1)custard{} over medium, whisking hard, until it boils and thickens, about ~{2%min}.

>> step: beat in the butter
Beat @unsalted butter{2%Tbs}(28 g) into @&(~1)hot pastry cream{}.

>> step: strain, then chill 2 hr
Strain @&(~1)pastry cream{} into a bowl, press plastic wrap onto the surface, and chill for ~{2%hr}.
